   "id": "wa-desu",
   "title": "X は Y です: X is Y",
   "explain": "は (written ha, read wa) marks the topic: what the sentence is about. です at the end makes it a polite statement, like 'is / am / are'. Japanese drops 'I' when it's obvious: 学生です alone means 'I'm a student'.",
